{
  "suite": "audio-decode",
  "description": "End-to-end: WAV file -> decoded messages. Supported formats: integer PCM 8/16/24/32-bit and IEEE float 32/64-bit, plain or WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE; unknown chunks are skipped; the first channel is decoded. The WAV file name carries the recording's local start time.",
  "normative": true,
  "compare": {
    "method": "Decode the whole file. message_count and every message's symbols MUST match exactly (hence parsed fields too); the symbols run from the first format specifier through the last ECC, the call's or the expansion's (F-25); utc_epoch within the tolerance (the instant the message starts, from the file-name base time plus sample position).",
    "utc_epoch_tolerance_s": 1
  },
  "cases": [
